Convex 1.41.0. A subscription is active at sequence 1, and no receipt exists for event "evt-2". An HTTP action awaits ctx.runMutation(internal.probe.applyThenFail, ...) with that subscription's ID and eventId "evt-2". It catches the error and responds with HTTP 500. No other writes occur.

convex/probe.ts
```ts
import { internalMutation } from "./_generated/server";
import { v } from "convex/values";
export const applyThenFail = internalMutation({
  args: { eventId: v.string(), subscriptionId: v.id("subscriptions") },
  handler: async (ctx, args) => {
    await ctx.db.patch(args.subscriptionId, { state: "canceled", sequence: 2 });
    await ctx.db.insert("receipts", { eventId: args.eventId, outcome: "applied" });
    throw new Error("processing failed");
  },
});
```
